EXT. FROZEN LAKE - ICE-FISHING HUT - DAY

A tin-roofed shack no bigger than a garden shed squats on a plain of white ice. Smoke curls from a stovepipe. Beyond it, the lake runs out to a horizon of pale, quiet sky.

INT. ICE-FISHING HUT - CONTINUOUS

Six people crowd a space meant for two. A stove glows orange in one corner. Four holes bored in the plank floor reveal black water below.

NANA PHILOMENA DUBOIS, 70s, sits in a lawn chair in a quilted parka, a fishing line wrapped around her gloved finger like a ring. Beside her, ARJUN CHAUDHRY, 40s, her son-in-law, tends the stove with the grim pride of a man who has built his first fire. TEDDY LINDGREN, 9, kneels on an overturned bucket, nose to the water. UNCLE SIONE TAUFA, 50s, enormous in a down jacket, wedges himself on a cooler, fiddling with a transistor radio. MEI-LING DUBOIS-CHAUDHRY, 35, hands out thermoses. And BEATRIZ, 5, lies on her stomach on the plank floor, one mitten dipping toward a hole.

MEI-LING
Beatriz, away from the water.

BEATRIZ
It's looking at me.

NANA PHILOMENA
That is a fish, child. They look at everyone.

UNCLE SIONE
Nana, don't scare her. It could be a very friendly fish.

TEDDY
It's not a fish. It's a muskrat.

ARJUN
(from the stove)
It can't be a muskrat. They don't live under ice.

TEDDY
This one does.

A tug on Nana's line. She sits bolt upright. Everyone stills. The line twitches again.

NANA PHILOMENA
Hush, all of you. Hush.

ARJUN
Philomena, I think you've got something.

MEI-LING
Mama, pull!

UNCLE SIONE ^
Pull, Nana, pull!

Nana hauls on the line with both hands. A silver fish the length of her forearm bursts through the hole, flops across the plank, and lands in Beatriz's lap. Beatriz shrieks. Teddy dives for it. Mei-Ling grabs Beatriz. Arjun knocks over the bucket. Uncle Sione catches the radio before it hits the stove.

BEATRIZ
It's alive!

TEDDY
It's a pike!

NANA PHILOMENA
It is dinner.

The fish flaps. Teddy pins it with both hands, grinning. Arjun kneels beside him, awkward, and takes the pliers from his belt.

ARJUN
Hold still. Hold still, little guy.

MEI-LING
Do you know how to do this?

ARJUN
I watched a video.

UNCLE SIONE
Give me the pliers, brother.

Arjun surrenders the pliers. Uncle Sione works the hook free in one practiced twist, then lifts the fish high in the cramped air for everyone to see. They cheer. The little hut rings with it.
